# Feature-loop gate

The live workflow is the feature loop — see `docs/systems/feature-loop.md`.
The old PIV loop (`docs/systems/agentic-coding.md`) is historical; use it only
for optional tiny Cursor-only work, not as what Hermes or the Cursor parent
runs.

For any task touching 2 or more files, run the feature loop:

Ready → specify → clarify → confirm → plan → tasks → [analyze] →
implement ↔ converge → critic → tester → UAT (human) → pr-review → publish.
Ready, critic, tester, and pr-reviewer use the AiNative agents under
`docs/agents/`; the Spec Kit stages use the project skills.

1. **Spec Kit stages** — specify / clarify / plan / tasks run as separate
   worker sessions; each worker knows only its step
   ([feature-loop.md](docs/systems/feature-loop.md)). Optional historical
   help: run the [scout](docs/agents/scout/) agent (System Understanding Brief + on-demand Repo Q&A on a cheap Tier 3 model) so the planner does not index the repo itself. Then assess complexity and ask **5 / 10 / 20** multiple-choice questions (**exactly 4 options each**) and recommend one answer per question; wait for confirmation. Before proposing new code: check **library** (worth adopting?) → **in-repo reuse** → **build from scratch**; document the choice in the execution plan. The written plan must include: execution plan, **acceptance criteria**, **validation layer** (for critic/tester), **test flows** (user-facing steps), and commit plan. The planner then **automatically runs the [plan-reviewer](docs/agents/plan-reviewer/) gate** (same model as the planner) and fixes/rewrites on REJECT until ACCEPT. Present the plan and wait for confirmation before implementing.
2. **Implementation** — execute one work item at a time; small atomic commits.
3. **Validation** — run the [critic](docs/agents/critic/) agent (adversarial review of plan + implementation), then the [tester](docs/agents/tester/) agent (execute the Plan's test flows) in a **new chat** with a **different model** than Plan or Implementation. See [validation-layer.md](docs/systems/validation-layer.md). Loop back to Implementation on fixable failures, or to Plan on a misunderstanding.
4. **PR review** — only after Validation passes, run the [pr-reviewer](docs/agents/pr-reviewer/) agent as the final gate. A surprise at PR review means the Validation layer missed something.

Do not write code before the Plan is confirmed. If the task is ambiguous, ask one clarifying question before planning.

Single-file tasks and typo/config fixes are exempt.
